{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G6ABz8qXCkd1i6U4rNqvdJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\timport Mathlib\n2\t\n3\topen MeasureTheory\n4\topen scoped ENNReal\n5\topen scoped EuclideanGeometry\n6\t\n7\tnoncomputable abbrev putnam_2024_a5_solution : Set ℝ := {0}\n8\t/--\n9\tConsider a circle $\\Omega$ with radius $9$ and center at the origin $(0, 0)$ and a disk $\\Delta$ with radius $1$ and center at $(r, 0)$ where $0 \\le r \\le 8$. Two points $P$ and $Q$ are chosen independently and uniformly at random\n10\ton $\\Omega$. Which value(s) of $r$ minimize the probability that the chord $\\overline{PQ}$ intersects $\\Delta$?\n11\t-/\n12\ttheorem putnam_2024_a5\n13\t    (IsIntersecting : ℝ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2) → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2) → Prop)\n14\t    (IsIntersecting_def : ∀ r P Q,\n15\t      IsIntersecting r P Q ↔ (line[ℝ,P,Q] : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)))\n16\t      ∩ Metric.sphere ((WithLp.equiv _ _).symm ![r, 0]) 1 ≠ ∅)\n17\t    (ProbIntersect : ℝ → ℝ≥0∞)\n18\t    (ProbIntersect_def : ∀ r,\n19\t      ProbIntersect r = volume {(s, t) : ℝ × ℝ | s ∈ Set.Icc 0 1 ∧ t ∈ Set.Icc 0 1 ∧\n20\t        IsIntersecting r\n21\t          ((WithLp.equiv _ _).symm ![9 * Real.cos (2 * Real.pi * s), 9 * Real.sin (2 * Real.pi * s)])\n22\t          ((WithLp.equiv _ _).symm ![9 * Real.cos (2 * Real.pi * t), 9 * Real.sin (2 * Real.pi * t)]) }) :\n23\t    {r | r ∈ Set.Icc 0 8 ∧ ProbIntersect r = ⨅ x ∈ Set.Icc 0 8, ProbIntersect x} =\n24\t      putnam_2024_a5_solution :=\n25\t  sorry\n26\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b84a8281-ac89-4e8a-8e5a-599ee3fe2166","uuid":"5ded5432-cb73-457b-813b-00f42c307234","timestamp":"2026-10-14T03:11:33.668Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/work/putnam_2024_a5.lean","content":"import Mathlib\n\nopen MeasureTheory\nopen scoped ENNReal\nopen scoped EuclideanGeometry\n\nnoncomputable abbrev putnam_2024_a5_solution : Set ℝ := {0}\n/--\nConsider a circle $\\Omega$ with radius $9